<h1>Cookie Policy — Moja Wioska</h1>

<p><strong>Effective date:</strong> 11 November 2026</p>

<p>This Cookie Policy explains how the "Moja Wioska" application (hereinafter: "App") and its associated website use cookies and similar technologies.</p>

<h2>1. What are cookies</h2>

<p>Cookies are small text files stored on the User's device by a web browser. They are used to remember preferences, maintain login sessions and analyse how services are used.</p>

<h2>2. Types of cookies used</h2>

<h3>2.1 Essential (technical) cookies</h3>
<p>Required for the proper functioning of the website and the App. These include:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Authentication session cookies</strong> — maintaining the login session (Firebase Authentication).</li>
  <li><strong>Language preference cookies</strong> — remembering the chosen interface language (Polish or English).</li>
</ul>

<h3>2.2 Functional cookies</h3>
<p>Allow the website to remember User settings and preferences for a better experience:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Display preferences</strong> — remembering interface settings.</li>
  <li><strong>Recently visited modules</strong> — quick access to recently used features.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2.3 Local data storage</h3>
<p>In addition to cookies the App uses local storage technologies:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>IndexedDB (Dexie)</strong> — a local database enabling offline mode. Stores tasks, recipes, shopping lists, notes and other User data on the device.</li>
  <li><strong>LocalStorage</strong> — stores minor preferences and application settings.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Third-party cookies</h2>

<p>The App and the website may use cookies set by external services:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Firebase (Google LLC)</strong> — cookies related to authentication and analytics. Google's privacy policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Google Play</strong> — if the User visits the Google Play store page from a link in the App, Google may set its own cookies in accordance with its policy.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Managing cookies</h2>

<h3>4.1 In the browser</h3>
<p>Users can manage cookies through their browser settings:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Block all or selected cookies.</li>
  <li>Delete stored cookies.</li>
  <li>Receive notifications before a cookie is saved.</li>
</ul>
<p>Disabling essential cookies may prevent the website from functioning properly.</p>

<h3>4.2 In the App</h3>
<p>Local data (IndexedDB, LocalStorage) can be removed by:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Clearing the App's data in Android device settings.</li>
  <li>Uninstalling and reinstalling the App.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Retention period</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Session cookies</strong> — deleted when the browser is closed or the User signs out.</li>
  <li><strong>Functional cookies</strong> — stored until manually deleted or expired (typically up to 1 year).</li>
  <li><strong>Local data (IndexedDB)</strong> — stored until the App's data is cleared or the account is deleted.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Cookie consent</h2>

<p>The website informs the User about the use of cookies on their first visit. Continued use of the website constitutes consent to the use of cookies as described in this Policy.</p>

<p>Essential cookies do not require consent as they are necessary for the service to function.</p>

<h2>7. Changes to this Cookie Policy</h2>

<p>We will notify Users of material changes to this Cookie Policy through the website or the App.</p>

